       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. DA5CALLMAIN.
      *> DA5 - A GROUP WHOSE ONLY NON-CHARACTER LEAF IS BINARY/PACKED
      *> CROSSES A CALL BOUNDARY. V59 GAVE SUCH A LEAF ITS PINNED BYTE
      *> IMAGE, AND RecordStructEmitter EMITS AsImage()/FromImage() FOR
      *> EXACTLY THAT PREDICATE (IsImageCapable) - BUT THE CALL GUARD
      *> WAS LEFT ON THE PRE-V59 IsCharacterImage, SO IT LOUD-STAGED A
      *> CALL WHOSE CODEC HAD ACTUALLY BEEN GENERATED. THE GROUP BELOW
      *> ANSWERED BYTE-LENGTH = 5 AND THEN THREW "NO WHOLE-GROUP
      *> CHARACTER IMAGE" ON THE CALL. THAT CLAIM WAS FALSE.
      *>
      *> 14.2.3 GR8 - "IF THE ARGUMENT IS PASSED BY REFERENCE, THE
      *> ACTIVATED RUNTIME ELEMENT OPERATES AS IF THE FORMAL PARAMETER
      *> OCCUPIES THE SAME STORAGE AREA AS THE ARGUMENT." COBOL.NET
      *> REALIZES THAT ALIASING THROUGH THE IMAGE ROUND-TRIP, SO THIS
      *> MUST CARRY THE COMP VALUE *IN* AND THE CALLEE'S WRITES *BACK
      *> OUT*. TESTING ONLY THAT IT NO LONGER THROWS WOULD MISS A
      *> BROKEN ROUND-TRIP, WHICH IS WHY BOTH DIRECTIONS ARE CHECKED.
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01 G.
          05 N PIC S9(4) COMP VALUE 1234.
          05 P PIC 9(3) COMP-3 VALUE 567.
          05 A PIC X(3) VALUE "abc".
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       MAIN.
      *> 2 BYTES BINARY + 2 BYTES PACKED (3 DIGITS -> 3/2+1) + 3 = 7.
           DISPLAY "LEN=" FUNCTION BYTE-LENGTH(G)
           DISPLAY "PRE  N=" N " P=" P " A=" A
           CALL "DA5CALLSUB" USING G
           DISPLAY "POST N=" N " P=" P " A=" A
           STOP RUN.
       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. DA5CALLSUB.
       DATA DIVISION.
       LINKAGE SECTION.
       01 LG.
          05 LN PIC S9(4) COMP.
          05 LP PIC 9(3) COMP-3.
          05 LA PIC X(3).
       PROCEDURE DIVISION USING LG.
       SUBMAIN.
           DISPLAY "SUB  N=" LN " P=" LP " A=" LA
           MOVE 7777 TO LN
           MOVE 890 TO LP
           MOVE "xyz" TO LA
           GOBACK.
